  "description": "The coordinator of a swarm of worker processes spread across many hosts. The library owns its own web host, so a desktop application can be the coordinator: it opens two authenticated, one-way message hubs - one for the Hives that manage each host, one for the Workers that do the work - mints the access tokens, which are different for each of the two roles, sends application-defined messages to everything connected to either hub, reports how many of each are connected, and tells them when the work is over. Pair it with CodeBrix.Swarm.Hive and CodeBrix.Swarm.Worker, and install all three at the same version.",
